# Task Triage

**First on every task**, before any other rule, tool call, or answer: score the work and print the
verdict. `docs/ai/model-policy.md` is the canon - the rubric, the thresholds, the adjustments and the
gate commands live there and nowhere else. This rule is only the pointer.

Five axes, 0-2 each, summed to 0-10: **blast radius, ambiguity, risk, verification, unknowns**. Report
the digits, not just the total.

```
Triage 6/10 (radius 2 · ambiguity 1 · risk 1 · verify 2 · unknowns 0)
Harness: Cursor · Model: <role, or the name you can verify> · Effort: high
Delegation: none · Gate: no · Context: 3 named files
Budget: ~120k output · Stop when: tests green and the gate set passes
```

Then one sentence on the cheapest thing the maintainer could say that would lower the score.

Three rules that matter more than the table:

- **Escalate context before escalating the model.** A cheap model with the right three files beats a
  frontier model with none.
- **Repeated failure is not a reason to escalate.** Two failed attempts mean the diagnosis is wrong.
- **Ambiguity scored 2 goes to the grilling gate before any edit**, whatever the total.

**Model names are not written here.** Cursor's picker belongs to the maintainer, and this repository has
not verified Cursor's model list - so report the role (cheapest / mid / frontier) and let the maintainer
map it. A model name written from memory is how the wrong model gets picked, and nothing fails when it
happens. Fill the row in `docs/ai/model-policy.md` once the list has actually been read.

Skip the verdict block for questions about the conversation, one-word confirmations, and
unchanged-scope continuations. Say "re-triage" and print a fresh block when the scope changes.
